# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The College's site was published on Google Sites at
# sites.google.com/uic.edu.ph/collegeofengineeringandarchi, and that address is
# linked from the University site and from Facebook. The paths below are the
# legacy ones mapped onto this site's routes, so any address already in
# circulation keeps working.
#
# Syntax: /from  /to  [status]. Status defaults to 200 (a rewrite); 301 is used
# throughout because these replacements are permanent.
#
# A rule may never name its own destination. Cloudflare matches the incoming
# path against these lines before it looks for a file, so `/events  /events
# 301` answers with a redirect to the address the visitor just asked for and the
# browser gives up with ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS. A route that already exists at
# its own address therefore gets no line here at all: Pages serves
# `dist/events-and-retreats/index.html` for `/events-and-retreats` and for
# `/events-and-retreats/` on its own, with no redirect involved.
#
# This file is only read by Cloudflare. The local preview serves dist through
# Caddy, which uses `try_files` and never parses these rules — so a loop here is
# invisible at http://cea.kube and total in production. scripts/verify-dist.py
# checks it; see the self-redirect test there.

# About.
#
# "CEA Logo & Seal" is the only child of the About menu with a page of its own
# under the design's own `data-path`; "Our Pride" sits at /about/our-pride for
# symmetry with it.
/about-cea/cea-logo-seal            /about/cea-logo-and-seal  301
/about-cea/our-pride                /about/our-pride          301
/about-cea/scholarships-offered     /scholarships-offered     301
/about-cea                          /about/our-pride          301

# Programmes. The legacy slugs are the design's `data-path` values, so the four
# programme routes are the paths the design already named.
/programs-offered/bs-architecture            /programs/bs-architecture             301
/programs-offered/bs-civil-engineering       /programs/bs-civil-engineering        301
/programs-offered/bs-computer-engineering    /programs/bs-computer-engineering     301
/programs-offered/bs-electronics-engineering /programs/bs-electronics-engineering  301
/programs-offered                   /programs                            301

# Featured Works. The legacy site filed works under a school year. The works
# themselves are now on one page and only one of the three states a year, so
# all three years resolve to the full set rather than to two empty archives.
/featured-works/sy-2024-2025  /featured-works  301
/featured-works/sy-2025-2026  /featured-works  301
/featured-works/sy-2026-2027  /featured-works  301

# Events & Retreats. The design gave this section a menu of four pages
# (events-and-retreats, engineering-week, spiritual-formation-retreats and
# archives) and screens for one of them. The other three addresses therefore
# resolve to the one page rather than dead-ending; if any of them is ever
# designed, its own route takes the line back and this page stops answering for
# it.
#
# The legacy /archives at the foot of this file is a different thing: it is the
# old Google Sites downloads-and-archives address, and it stays with the works
# archive.
#
# /events-and-retreats is deliberately absent. The page is served from its own
# address with no rule.
/events                            /events-and-retreats  301
/engineering-week                  /events-and-retreats  301
/spiritual-formation-retreats      /events-and-retreats  301

# Contact. The design's contact band is a page here as well as a homepage
# section, so the legacy address lands on it directly. The page's own address
# needs no line either.
/contact                      /contact-and-inquiries  301

# The legacy faculty roster, the downloads index and the archives. None of these
# have a page on this site: the design carries no faculty listing, no documents
# and no separate archive. They are redirected rather than left to 404 so a
# legacy link reaches the closest real page instead of a dead end.
/faculty                      /about/our-pride          301
/archives                     /featured-works           301
/downloads                    /featured-works           301
/home                         /                         301
